01:04:35,294 --> 01:04:41,294
All the Beauty and the Bloodshed is a 2022 American biographical documentary
film about photographer, artist, and activist Nan Goldin.

10
01:11:45,882 --> 01:11:51,882
The film is produced, co-edited and directed by Laura Poitras, and tackles Goldin's life through her advocacy during the HIV/AIDS crisis
in the ‘80s, and her fight against the Sackler family for their role in the current opioid epidemic in the United States.

11
01:18:56,470 --> 01:19:02,470
Poitras, a long-time friend and fan, stated that "Nan's art and vision has inspired my work for years, and has influenced generations of filmmakers."
The film premiered on September 3, 2022, at
the 79th Venice International Film Festival, where it was awarded the Golden Lion, making it the second documentary (following Sacro GRA in 2013) to win the top prize at Venice.

12
01:26:07,058 --> 01:26:13,058
It also screened at the 2022 New York Film Festival, where it was the festival's
centerpiece film and for which Goldin designed two official posters.

13
01:33:17,647 --> 01:33:23,647
The film was received with critical acclaim, and was
released in cinemas by Neon on November 23, 2022.

14
01:40:28,235 --> 01:40:34,235
At the 95th Academy Awards, the film was nominated for Best Documentary Feature.

15
01:47:38,823 --> 01:47:44,823
The film then went on to win a Peabody Award at the 84th ceremony for "capturing the zeal of
an artist eager to use her work to create a new vision for and of the world."

16
01:54:49,411 --> 01:54:55,411
The film explores themes of aids, photographer,
photography, political activism, interview.
